---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="Full disclosure of our affiliate relationships. We earn commissions on some of the products we recommend — at no additional cost to readers."
>
  <section class="container-article py-12 md:py-16">
    <h1 class="font-heading font-extrabold text-4xl md:text-5xl text-navy-deep tracking-tight">
      Affiliate disclosure.
    </h1>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none mt-6">
      <p>
        The Finance Verdict participates in affiliate programs from a number of personal-finance
        product companies — budgeting apps, credit monitoring services, investing platforms,
        tax software, banks, and debt-management companies. When you click a link on this site
        and sign up through one of those programs, we may earn a commission at
        <strong>no additional cost to you</strong>.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>We will never recommend a tool we wouldn't use ourselves, even when the
        commission would be higher.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2>Brands with active or pending affiliate relationships</h2>
      <p>As of the current publication, we hold or are pursuing affiliate relationships with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Budgeting — YNAB, Monarch Money, Rocket Money, EveryDollar, Copilot, Tiller, Quicken, Simplifi</li>
        <li>Credit monitoring — Credit Karma, Experian, MyFICO, IdentityIQ, LifeLock, Identity Guard</li>
        <li>Investing — Empower (Personal Capital), M1 Finance, Wealthfront, Betterment, Robinhood</li>
        <li>Tax software — TurboTax, H&amp;R Block, FreeTaxUSA, Cash App Taxes, TaxSlayer, TaxAct</li>
        <li>Banking and savings — SoFi, Marcus by Goldman Sachs, Ally, Discover, Capital One, Chime</li>
        <li>Debt management — National Debt Relief, Freedom Debt Relief, Accredited Debt Relief</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Most of these are managed via affiliate networks (Impact, CJ Affiliate, FlexOffers,
        ShareASale, Rakuten). A handful are direct partnerships.
      </p>

      <h2>How affiliate links are marked</h2>
      <p>
        All outbound links to affiliate partners are marked with <code>rel="sponsored"</code>
        in the HTML — the standard signal Google requests for affiliate links — and open in a
        new tab.
      </p>

      <h2>How recommendations are ranked</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>We rank by what fits the use case, not by commission size.</strong> If two
        budgeting apps offer similar features but one pays $30 per signup and another pays
        $80, we recommend whichever is better for the reader.
      </p>
      <p>
        For example: a $0/year FreeTaxUSA filing is sometimes the right pick over a $189
        TurboTax filing, even though the TurboTax commission would be larger. The
        recommendation tracks what you should do, not what would pay us.
      </p>

      <h2>What this affiliate revenue funds</h2>
      <p>
        Affiliate commissions fund the editorial and testing work behind this site. We don't
        run paid advertising or sponsored content. We don't share our email subscribers with
        affiliate partners.
      </p>

      <h2>No financial-credential collection</h2>
      <p>
        We do not collect bank account credentials, Social Security numbers, or any other
        sensitive financial information on this site. When you click an affiliate link, you
        connect directly with the product company under their own privacy and security
        policies. We never see your account data.
      </p>

      <h2>FTC compliance</h2>
      <p>
        This disclosure exists in compliance with the U.S. Federal Trade Commission's "Guides
        Concerning the Use of Endorsements and Testimonials in Advertising" (16 CFR Part 255).
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        If you have any questions about how we handle affiliate relationships,{" "}
        <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
